  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "He is white robed and solemn-looking.",
      "chapters": [
        2183
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance-and-rank",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Historical records place Giant Sun Immortal Venerable’s life at over eight thousand years, a middle to upper result among rank nine venerables, while Red Lotus Demon Venerable lived only three thousand and other venerables generally around seven thousand. Primordial Origin Immortal Venerable’s own lifespan was the longest of them all, twenty-five thousand years.",
      "chapters": [
        601
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance-and-rank",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable",
        "char_red_lotus_demon_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Venerable is rank nine. Demon Venerable names a rank nine demonic path Gu Master; Immortal Venerable names a rank nine righteous Gu Master.",
      "chapters": [
        383
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance-and-rank",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master",
        "sys_righteous_path"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Led by him, Central Continent was already reformed during the Remote Antiquity Era, establishing the sect system.",
      "chapters": [
        704
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "founding-acts",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_central_continent",
        "evt_era_remote"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan names him the first rank nine Gu Immortal in human history and the creator of Central Continent’s Heavenly Court, a force that has stood through many eras. Fang Yuan also credits him with the teaching phrase that man is the spirit of all living beings and Gu are the essence of heaven and earth, spoken to educate later people and aid inheritances of various paths.",
      "chapters": [
        821
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "founding-acts",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_gu_venerable",
        "fac_heavenly_court"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The first generation Heavenly Court Immortal King was Primordial Origin Immortal Venerable, a qi path cultivator. Heavenly Court still holds the foundation of his immortal aperture together with later venerables’ work.",
      "chapters": [
        2001
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "founding-acts",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He led humanity’s uprising and founded Heavenly Court.",
      "chapters": [
        2083
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "founding-acts",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Even with Ren Zu, Ren Zu’s ten children, and both Primordial Origin Immortal Venerable and Star Constellation Immortal Venerable, humans remained few while variant humans controlled most of the world in the Immemorial and Remote Antiquity Eras.",
      "chapters": [
        871
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "historical-background",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ren_zu",
        "char_star_constellation_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "During the Remote Antiquity Era the two Immortal Venerables appeared and led humans to resist variant human rule, establishing human authority.",
      "chapters": [
        912
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "historical-background",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Three million years ago in the Remote Antiquity Era the roster lists Primordial Origin Immortal Venerable, then Star Constellation Immortal Venerable.",
      "chapters": [
        2085
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "historical-background",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Star Constellation Immortal Venerable is the second venerable in history, a disciple of Primordial Origin Immortal Venerable, and the second generation Immortal King of Heavenly Court.",
      "chapters": [
        984
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "historical-background",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the Remote Antiquity Era he created qi path and enslavement path, while Star Constellation Immortal Venerable created wisdom path and star path.",
      "chapters": [
        1323
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "historical-background",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "path_wisdom"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Heavenly Court immortal recounts that he prepared the Immortal Gu House Embroidered Tower as dowry for Star Constellation Immortal Venerable’s betrothal.",
      "chapters": [
        1010
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "historical-background",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "house_embroidered_tower"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Triple qi retraction, the qi path killer move Duke Long uses against Purple Mountain True Monarch, was created by Primordial Origin Immortal Venerable.",
      "chapters": [
        1367
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "triple-qi-retraction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_duke_long",
        "char_purple_mountain_true_monarch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He lies on the bed quietly, eyes shut, expression plain, with a faint smile at the corners of his lips. He has died, having concealed how severe his injuries were and spent the last of his strength on a human path killer move that his disciple then names lying in bed.",
      "chapters": [
        2328
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heavenly Court grows a qi harvest fruit to revive him, following his own original plan, and the fruit brings that revival almost to completion before Star Constellation Immortal Venerable kneels and pays respects to her master. At the next moment Primordial Origin Immortal Venerable explodes.",
      "chapters": [
        2328
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "revival-and-explosion",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
